---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service — WifiHeatmap">
    <header class="w-full border-b border-cyan-500/10 bg-[#050814]/80 backdrop-blur-md sticky top-0 z-50">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-6 h-18 flex items-center justify-between">
            <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`} class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <img
                    src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/icon.png`}
                    alt="WifiHeatmap Icon"
                    class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl object-contain shadow-sm"
                />
                <span class="text-xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">WifiHeatmap</span>
            </a>
            <a
                href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`}
                class="text-sm font-semibold text-cyan-400 hover:text-cyan-300 transition-colors"
            >
                ← Back to Home
            </a>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main class="pt-16 pb-24 bg-[#050814]">
        <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
            <div class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
                <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-cyan-950/60 border border-cyan-500/30 text-cyan-300 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
                    <span>Terms & End User Agreement</span>
                </div>
                <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4">
                    Terms of Service
                </h1>
                <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm">
                    Effective Date: September 2026 • WifiHeatmap for Android
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-10 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed text-base">
                <!-- Section 1 -->
                <section class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">1. Agreement to Terms & License</h2>
                    <p>
                        By installing, downloading, or using the <strong>WifiHeatmap</strong> mobile application or website, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        WifiHeatmap grants you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the application on your supported Android devices in accordance with these terms.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 2 -->
                <section class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">2. Permitted Use & Ethical Responsibilities</h2>
                    <p>
                        WifiHeatmap is designed and distributed exclusively as an RF diagnostics, channel optimization, and site survey utility. You agree to use the application strictly in compliance with all applicable local, national, and international laws:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-400">
                        <li><strong>Authorized Surveys:</strong> You should only conduct physical indoor heatmap surveys in facilities or properties where you have authorization to inspect wireless signals.</li>
                        <li><strong>No Hacking or Exploitation:</strong> WifiHeatmap is NOT a tool for intercepting private data packets, bypassing authentication, cracking passwords, or conducting unauthorized network intrusion. Any such modification or malicious deployment is strictly prohibited.</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 3 -->
                <section class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">3. Data Ownership & Local Storage</h2>
                    <p>
                        Any floor plans imported, measurements logged, or survey reports exported are your sole property. Because WifiHeatmap has no cloud synchronizer or remote database, you are solely responsible for backing up your local files, floorplans, and survey exports.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 4 -->
                <section class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">4. Disclaimer of Warranty</h2>
                    <p class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                        THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 5 -->
                <section class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">5. Hardware & Sensor Dependencies</h2>
                    <p>
                        Certain advanced features—such as 6 GHz frequency scanning (Wi-Fi 6E/7), 320 MHz channel detection, Wi-Fi RTT ranging (802.11mc), barometric altitude sensing, and step detector hardware—depend directly on the capabilities of your Android device's hardware chipset and operating system level.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <!-- Section 6 -->
                <section class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">6. Inquiries & Support</h2>
                    <p>
                        For technical inquiries, bug reports, or support questions, please contact us via our official Google Play Store app listing:
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <a
                            href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.heymeowcat.wifiheatmap"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="text-cyan-400 hover:text-cyan-300 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4"
                        >
                            View WifiHeatmap on Google Play
                        </a>
                    </p>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
</Layout>
